1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,484
Visitors leave fields empty, and a form that accepts them collects nothing useful.

2
00:00:06,484 --> 00:00:11,593
In this video, you'll see how the Forms module validates what visitors type:

3
00:00:11,593 --> 00:00:16,890
the messages the form displays, and the workflow that finds the missing values.

4
00:00:21,490 --> 00:00:24,471
Validation in the Forms module has two parts.

5
00:00:24,471 --> 00:00:29,731
A workflow checks the submitted values and records an error for each one that fails.

6
00:00:29,731 --> 00:00:32,770
The form then displays the errors it receives.

7
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:35,969
A form can display errors in three ways.

8
00:00:35,969 --> 00:00:40,760
The Validation Summary widget lists them together, the Validation option of an input

9
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:45,179
shows a message under that input, and the Validation widget shows the message

10
00:00:45,179 --> 00:00:46,670
of any field you name.

11
00:00:47,420 --> 00:00:49,407
Visitors also need a way back.

12
00:00:49,407 --> 00:00:52,940
The form saves the page it is on, and after a failed check

13
00:00:52,940 --> 00:00:58,240
the workflow sends the visitor to that page, where the error messages are displayed again.

14
00:01:02,433 --> 00:01:04,183
Let's start with the form.

15
00:01:04,183 --> 00:01:06,862
This Contact Form page holds a Form widget.

16
00:01:06,862 --> 00:01:10,964
Its Save Form Location option is checked, so the form stores the page

17
00:01:10,964 --> 00:01:14,573
it sits on, ready for the workflow to send the visitor back.

18
00:01:15,029 --> 00:01:18,888
Each Input, Text Area and Select widget has a Validation option.

19
00:01:18,888 --> 00:01:22,692
Let's open the Name input and set it to Standard, so the widget

20
00:01:22,692 --> 00:01:25,229
shows its error message after the field.

21
00:01:25,682 --> 00:01:30,013
Set the Email input and the Message text area to Standard as well.

22
00:01:30,013 --> 00:01:33,742
The other choice, None, shows no message for that field.

23
00:01:34,194 --> 00:01:36,871
Next, the Validation Summary widget.

24
00:01:36,871 --> 00:01:39,294
Insert one above the Name input.

25
00:01:39,294 --> 00:01:44,584
It lists every error together, because Show Model Only Error stays unchecked.

26
00:01:45,041 --> 00:01:46,088
Click Publish.

27
00:01:46,088 --> 00:01:50,591
The form is ready to display errors, but nothing decides which values are wrong.

28
00:01:50,591 --> 00:01:52,581
That is the job of the workflow.

29
00:01:56,881 --> 00:02:00,617
Under Design, Workflows, open Contact Form Validation.

30
00:02:00,617 --> 00:02:04,976
It starts with an HTTP Request event set to POST, and the Action

31
00:02:04,976 --> 00:02:09,771
of the Form widget holds its URL, so the form submits to this workflow.

32
00:02:10,239 --> 00:02:13,486
Click the Done outcome and add Bind Form Model State.

33
00:02:13,486 --> 00:02:17,503
It keeps every submitted field, so the form can show again what the

34
00:02:17,503 --> 00:02:19,429
visitor typed after an error.

35
00:02:19,890 --> 00:02:22,303
Add Validate Form Field after it.

36
00:02:22,303 --> 00:02:26,449
Field Name is the HTML Name of the input to check, here Name,

37
00:02:26,449 --> 00:02:29,357
and Error Message is the text to display.

38
00:02:29,357 --> 00:02:34,430
The activity records an error when that field is empty or holds only spaces.

39
00:02:34,922 --> 00:02:37,094
The activity has three outcomes:

40
00:02:37,094 --> 00:02:38,809
Done, Valid and Invalid.

41
00:02:38,809 --> 00:02:42,810
Done always follows, so here it leads to the next check, and the

42
00:02:42,810 --> 00:02:45,382
fields are checked one after the other.

43
00:02:45,836 --> 00:02:49,500
Add the checks for Email and Message in the same way, each from

44
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:51,677
the Done outcome of the one before.

45
00:02:51,677 --> 00:02:55,660
Each has its own Field Name and Error Message, which the editor saves

46
00:02:55,660 --> 00:02:57,306
when you leave the field.

47
00:03:00,013 --> 00:03:02,685
After the last check, add Validate Form.

48
00:03:02,685 --> 00:03:04,893
It looks for any recorded error:

49
00:03:04,893 --> 00:03:08,553
with none it follows Valid, otherwise it follows Invalid.

50
00:03:09,017 --> 00:03:12,583
From Invalid, add HTTP Redirect To Form Location.

51
00:03:12,583 --> 00:03:16,926
It sends the visitor back to the page the form saved, and the

52
00:03:16,926 --> 00:03:19,130
error messages go with them.

53
00:03:19,130 --> 00:03:24,187
Its Form Location Key stays empty, since this workflow handles one form.

54
00:03:24,663 --> 00:03:29,622
From Valid, add HTTP Redirect and set its Location to the thank-you page

55
00:03:29,622 --> 00:03:33,563
of the site, so a visitor whose values pass lands there.

56
00:03:34,015 --> 00:03:36,914
Fit to content shows the whole workflow.

57
00:03:36,914 --> 00:03:38,174
Click Publish:

58
00:03:38,174 --> 00:03:42,775
a draft never runs, so the form starts the published workflow only.

59
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:51,067
On the Contact Form page, let's submit the form with nothing typed.

60
00:03:51,067 --> 00:03:55,349
The page reloads, and the summary above the Name field lists one message

61
00:03:55,349 --> 00:03:57,160
for each field that failed.

62
00:03:57,614 --> 00:04:04,504
Each message also appears under its own field, because each input uses the Standard Validation option.

63
00:04:04,954 --> 00:04:07,179
Let's type a name and submit again.

64
00:04:07,179 --> 00:04:11,086
The name is still in its field, because Bind Form Model State kept

65
00:04:11,086 --> 00:04:13,854
it, and only Email and Message report errors.

66
00:04:14,312 --> 00:04:17,859
Fill in the email address and the message, and submit.

67
00:04:17,859 --> 00:04:23,772
Every check passes, the workflow follows Valid, and the visitor arrives on the thank-you page.

68
00:04:25,772 --> 00:04:29,669
Validation in the Forms module is a workflow that records errors and a

69
00:04:29,669 --> 00:04:31,208
form that displays them.

70
00:04:31,208 --> 00:04:32,542
Thanks for watching.

